      "i_do_script": "Now I'm going to turn a phrase into an actual expression. 'Nine more than a number' — I know 'more than' means add. The number I'm adding is 9, and 'a number' becomes my variable n. So I write n + 9. Watch the order: 'five less than a number' means I start with the number and subtract 5, so it's n − 5, NOT 5 − n. The variable comes first when the phrase says 'less than.'",
      "canonical_error": {
        "pattern": "Reverses the order of subtraction — writes 5 − n instead of n − 5 for 'five less than a number'",
        "example": "Student writes 3 − x for 'three less than x' instead of x − 3",
        "why": "English word order ('three less than x') puts the 3 first, so students write it first. But 'less than' means subtract FROM the number, so the variable comes first."
      },
      "item_template": "A verbal phrase with one operation and one variable. Student writes the algebraic expression. EQ response (type the expression). Phrases use 'more than,' 'less than,' 'times,' or 'the quotient of.'",
      "sample_items": [
        {
          "stem": "Write an expression for: 'seven less than a number n'",
          "answer": "n - 7",
          "choices": null,
          "distractor_logic": "Common errors: 7 - n (reversed order), 7n (wrong operation), n + 7 (wrong operation)"
        },
        {
          "stem": "Write an expression for: 'the product of 4 and a number x'",
          "answer": "4x",
          "choices": null,
          "distractor_logic": "Common errors: 4 + x (wrong operation), x/4 (wrong operation), x⁴ (confuses product with power)"
        },
        {
          "stem": "Write an expression for: 'a number y divided by 3'",
          "answer": "y/3",
          "choices": null,
          "distractor_logic": "Common errors: 3/y (reversed), 3y (wrong operation), y - 3 (wrong operation)"
        }
      ],
      "redirect_script": {
        "stop": "Let's check your expression by testing it with a number.",
        "prompt": "Try plugging in a number. If the phrase is 'seven less than a number' and the number is 10, should the answer be 3 or -3? Since 10 minus 7 is 3, the expression must be n − 7, not 7 − n. Does your expression give the right answer?",
        "praise": "Your expression works! You got the order right, which is the trickiest part of writing expressions."
      },
      "worked_example_script": [
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "text": "Watch how I turn a verbal phrase into a math expression."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "text": "The phrase is: 'seven less than a number n.'"
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "text": "I underline the key words: 'less than.' That tells me to subtract."
        },
        {
          "kind": "ask",
          "text": "When the phrase says 'less than,' which comes first in the expression — the number or the variable?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "text": "'Less than' means I start with the variable and subtract from it. So n comes first, then minus 7."
        },
        {
          "kind": "show",
          "text": "Write n - 7 in the answer box."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "text": "I check by plugging in: if n is 10, then n - 7 is 3, which matches 'seven less than 10.'"
        },
        {
          "kind": "watch",
          "text": "If a student writes 7 - n, they reversed the order because the 7 was said first. Stop and re-read the phrase, then test with a number to show the order matters."
        }
      ],
      "printable_artifact": {
        "title": "Write one-operation expressions from verbal phrases Reference",
        "kind": "reference_card",
        "instructions": "Keep this nearby until you have these patterns memorized. The variable usually comes first when the phrase says 'less than' or 'divided by.'",
        "items": [
          "the sum of n and 8  ->  n + 8",
          "5 more than x  ->  x + 5",
          "a number y increased by 12  ->  y + 12",
          "9 plus a number n  ->  9 + n",
          "7 less than a number n  ->  n - 7",
          "a number x decreased by 4  ->  x - 4",
          "the difference of y and 6  ->  y - 6",
          "n minus 10  ->  n - 10",
          "the product of 3 and y  ->  3y",
          "4 times a number x  ->  4x",
          "twice a number n  ->  2n",
          "6 multiplied by a number k  ->  6k",
          "a number y divided by 3  ->  y/3",
          "the quotient of n and 5  ->  n/5",
          "x split into 4 equal parts  ->  x/4",
          "a number n per 2  ->  n/2"
