      "redirect_script": {
        "stop": "Let's figure out which number repeats and which is a one-time thing.",
        "prompt": "Ask yourself: 'Which amount happens every time?' That's your rate — it gets multiplied by the variable. 'Which amount happens only once?' That's your constant — it gets added. In this problem, which number repeats?",
        "praise": "You identified the rate and the constant correctly. That's the key to writing expressions from word problems."
      },
      "worked_example_script": [
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "text": "Watch how I turn a real-world situation into an algebraic expression."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "text": "The problem says: a gym charges $25 per month plus a one-time $50 registration fee, and we want the total cost for m months."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "text": "I ask myself two questions. First: which amount repeats every month?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "ask",
          "text": "Which number happens every single month — the $25 or the $50?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "text": "The $25 repeats every month, so $25 gets multiplied by m. That gives me 25m."
        },
        {
          "kind": "ask",
          "text": "Now which amount only happens one time?"
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "text": "The $50 registration fee happens once, so it's added on at the end as a constant. The expression is 25m + 50."
        },
        {
          "kind": "show",
          "text": "Circle 25m + 50 as the answer and underline 'per month' and 'one-time' in the problem."
        },
        {
          "kind": "watch",
          "text": "If a student writes 50m + 25, they swapped the rate and the constant — they made the one-time fee repeat. Stop and ask, 'Does the registration fee happen every month, or just once?'"
        }
      ],
      "printable_artifact": {
        "title": "Write expressions from real-world contexts Reference",
        "kind": "reference_card",
        "instructions": "Keep this nearby. Match the wording in the problem to one of these patterns, then plug in the numbers.",
        "items": [
          "$P per item plus $F flat fee  ->  Pn + F   (e.g., $8 per pizza plus $3 delivery -> 8p + 3)",
          "$R per hour, already has $S saved  ->  Rh + S   (e.g., $15/hr, $40 saved -> 15h + 40)",
          "$M per month plus one-time $F signup  ->  Mx + F   (e.g., $25/mo + $50 signup -> 25m + 50)",
          "Starts with A, gains B each time  ->  A + Bn   (e.g., 100 points, +5 each level -> 100 + 5n)",
          "Starts with A, loses B each time  ->  A - Bn   (e.g., $200 saved, spends $20/wk -> 200 - 20w)",
          "X items shared equally among Y people  ->  X / Y   (e.g., 24 cookies, 6 kids -> 24/6)",
          "Total T split into groups of g  ->  T / g   (e.g., 30 students in groups of 5 -> 30/5)",
          "M miles at S miles per hour  ->  M / S hours   (e.g., 120 mi at 60 mph -> 120/60)",
          "N times as many as x  ->  Nx   (e.g., three times as many apples -> 3x)",
          "B more than x  ->  x + B   (e.g., 7 more than a number -> x + 7)",
          "B less than x  ->  x - B   (NOT B - x; e.g., 4 less than n -> n - 4)",
          "Twice a number, increased by C  ->  2x + C   (e.g., twice age plus 5 -> 2a + 5)",
          "Rule: the amount that REPEATS gets multiplied by the variable (the rate). The amount that happens ONCE gets added as a constant."
        ]
      }
    },
